comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T05:38:50.502Z","harness:claude-code","Measured 2026-08-07: a one-line refusal costs 1100 bytes of envelope.\n\nThe exact invocation that produced the release-blocking production error was replayed after its refusal was reclassified as a usage error. The refusal now exits 2 with a stable code, and the JSON envelope is 1100 bytes for a single sentence of diagnosis. The message itself appears twice, as title and as detail. The recovery bundle re-serializes the invocation three ways: the attempted command as one string, the normalized argument vector as ten separate array entries, and the provided flag names as a fourth list. The examples offered are the two most generic strings the product can emit, naming the root help and a placeholder command, neither of which addresses the refusal. Against a 9-byte version read, the cheapest thing this CLI can print, the refusal is 122 times larger, and against the 524-byte agent-token baseline recorded for this command it is more than double.\n\nThe observation for this item is that the three re-serializations are the bulk of the payload and none of them tells the caller anything the caller did not just type. The teachable content, the code and the one sentence that names what was wrong, is under 150 bytes.\n"
  "2026-08-14T07:55:44.969Z","harness:codex","Tranche evidence: health diagnostics now have a hard 100-warning collection bound and truthful completeness receipts; strict-exit selects summary, command-scoped contracts omit unrelated payload, and the mandatory omission receipt was shortened while preserving structured recovery. Token-surface and 109 linked health/contracts tests pass. Residual all-error-family ceilings and ten-path before/after corpus remain, so this item returns open."
  "2026-08-21T22:48:07.831Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-22: one coupled SDK/CLI/contract/assurance tranche will declare binding diagnostic ceilings, preserve corrective actions through deterministic degradation, replay the ten most frequent refusal paths in isolated trackers, and extend executable recovery evidence. Only these four actively edited items are claimed; all other backlog items remain unclaimed."
  "2026-08-21T23:58:52.681Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence (2026-08-22): shipped the first production diagnostic output-budget family across SDK, CLI rendering, runtime contracts, MCP parity, corpus governance, generated artifacts, and docs. Ten representative error/warning/validation/recovery paths are ratcheted by a production baseline and refusal-closure gate; all 10 preserve corrective action and stay within their declared budgets. Exact verification: pnpm lint passed; 7,717 tests at 100% statements/branches/functions/lines; 22/22 refusal probes; 10/10 diagnostic probes; security scan and pnpm audit clean; packed npx plus isolated Node and bunx consumers passed. The item remains active for its stated remaining exhaustive family/CLI-path and before/after measurement scope."
  "2026-08-22T00:51:50.951Z","harness:codex","Review follow-up (2026-08-22 UTC): CodeRabbit findings were reproduced and fixed for blank-only corrective actions, unknown diagnostic classes, prototype-sensitive own properties, projected-envelope typing, and unbounded omitted-field receipts. The PM test plan now carries exact commands and current run records: focused integration 77/77, recovery closure 22/22 plus diagnostics 10/10, exact coverage 56,428/56,428 statements, 42,152/42,152 branches, 11,725/11,725 functions, and 54,405/54,405 lines, tracker-context lint/static assurance, credential scan, dependency audit, package artifact, and packed npx smoke all passed. Timestamp clarification: the earlier comment labeled 2026-08-22 used the repository operator timezone Europe/Vienna; its stored 2026-08-21T23:58:52Z timestamp is 2026-08-22 local time."
  "2026-08-22T01:17:35.802Z","harness:codex","Timezone clarification: the implementation-start event stored at 2026-08-21T22:48:07.831Z is 2026-08-22 00:48:07.831 Europe/Vienna; the work began on the requested local date."
  "2026-08-22T01:47:36.782Z","harness:codex","Review evidence: second exact-head review fixes now cover malformed present receipts, UTF-8 byte-exact JSON/text ceilings, empty-recovery next-step fallback, safe own-property preservation, required text receipt typing, and runtime SDK exports. Full repository coverage passed 551 files / 7,721 tests at 100% statements (56,473/56,473), branches (42,192/42,192), functions (11,732/11,732), and lines (54,447/54,447)."
  "2026-08-22T02:01:58.115Z","harness:codex","Reviewed delivery evidence: PR #1083 merged exact reviewed head 4b5f645d3e2ff1e4de1d00eccfbc158f1eb9f3ee into main as e790cd0e12c2907998bcca8797c7ae3577f28d8f. All required exact-head hosted checks passed; the review inventory had zero unresolved threads after every actionable finding was fixed or evidence-backed declined, every bot comment received an explicit usefulness reaction, and the manual CodeRabbit rerun was rate-limited. Greptile was explicitly triggered but produced no check, review, or comment, so provider silence is recorded as a limitation rather than approval. Final packed-artifact verification passed from a fresh temporary consumer under Node and Bun with UTF-8 ceilings and corrective-action preservation. Full repository coverage passed 551 files and 7,721 tests at exact 100/100/100/100. This item returns to open and unclaimed because its documented exhaustive residual remains outside this delivered tranche."
  "2026-08-22T02:49:35.040Z","harness:codex","Release evidence 2026-08-22: production Auto Release run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/runs/32545649142 completed successfully and created immutable-source tag v2026.8.22 at d7b6f18ce912ccf84d754cf5e539b4090c62c98b. Tag-driven Release run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/runs/32546288241 completed successfully, published npm @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.22 with provenance, created the non-draft/non-prerelease GitHub release, finalized Sentry release pm-cli@2026.8.22 with 18 commits and zero new groups, and uploaded sourcemaps. Public verification passed GitHub/npm plus fresh npx and Bun 11-step installed-agent sessions; one first-attempt post-success temporary cleanup race was retried successfully and its known residual directory was safely removed. Post-release Sentry shows zero unresolved issues; the 14-day gate reports critical=0, high=0, ignored_noise=0, and ignored_expected_handled=0. Telemetry flush delivered 3/3 valid events with queue_progressed=true, queue_empty=true, zero invalid rows, and no failed flush. GitHub reports isImmutable=false, so immutability is policy/workflow-enforced through the exact tag SHA rather than platform-enforced. The item remains open and unclaimed for its already documented residual."
  "2026-08-22T04:33:19.066Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-22: extend the production diagnostic gate across all four declared diagnostic classes, persist per-probe before/after measurements, and require action-first bounded output through real CLI paths and SDK contracts. Duplicate check used the complete 2,533-item all-status corpus."
  "2026-08-22T06:05:52.360Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence 2026-08-22: all four declared diagnostic classes remain SDK contract data with binding JSON/text ceilings and a deterministic full-to-action-only degradation ladder. Structured refusals now carry compact identity fields and recovery-bearing errors use the recovery_bundle class; full suggested_retry_args is atomic under compaction. The ten-path governed corpus records original 9,328 versus emitted 6,639 estimated tokens, with all 10 within budget and all 10 retaining corrective action. Negative controls fail on unknown classes, blank actions, malformed receipts, UTF-8 byte overflow, missing baselines, and over-budget or action-losing diagnostics. Verification: diagnostic gate 10/10, refusal gate 117/117, focused 23/23, exact full coverage 553 files and 7,732 tests at 100 percent statements, branches, functions, and lines, plus full lint/static assurance, security scan, dependency audit, packed artifact, npx, and clean npm and Bun consumers. The item remains dependency-linked to open pm-5t33or, whose live comments still document a broader every-command residual; this evidence does not claim that parent scope is complete."
  "2026-08-22T06:14:15.426Z","harness:codex","Delivery PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1086 at implementation head 1fc2a16e2. Hosted checks and review providers are running against the SDK-first refusal, diagnostic, generated-contract, test, documentation, and reviewed PM closeout tranche."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T20:42:10.437Z","harness:claude-code","Measured diagnostic cost and its redundancy on the shipped 2026.7.25 build, so this item's ceilings can be set against real output. Isolated sandbox, one item present.\n\nPer-diagnostic sizes: get on an unknown id 447 B (~111 tokens); unknown mutating flag 725 B (~181); unknown command 668 B (~167); invalid multi-value filter 684 B (~171); close without a required argument 940 B (~235); unknown graph subcommand 711 B (~177); out-of-domain --confidence value 613 B (~153).\n\nThe range is modest, but roughly 40 percent of each envelope is literal repetition, which is the cheapest thing to reclaim before any ceiling is enforced. On the unknown-flag case (22 lines):\n- the message text appears twice verbatim, once after \"Error:\" and again under \"What happened:\";\n- the corrective command appears three times, as the Examples entry, as attempted_command, and as suggested_retry, with normalized_args carrying a fourth near-copy;\n- \"What is required\" and \"Why\" render generic contract prose that is identical across unrelated failures and carries no case-specific information.\n\nThat suggests the degradation order this item declares should drop the duplicated renderings before it ever truncates the corrective action, and that the smallest permitted budget can be well under the current sizes without losing a single fact. The related structural assertion — corrective action first — is already testable against this shape: the recovery bundle is last today, so an agent reads the full explanation before reaching the command it needs."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-21T23:59:01.664Z","harness:codex",Diagnostic budgets should not add receipt overhead when output already fits; degradation receipts become useful only when content is actually omitted or compacted. Corrective-action completeness can justify a larger default budget than the smallest representable diagnostic.
